/T (In this coding pattern, pointers are references to an array/list indexes. By using two pointers, we can process two elements at a time in a single loop. The two pointers iterate over an array/list in certain directions until some conditions are fulfilled and process two index elements simultaneously. The pattern is often used when - )
/E (In this coding pattern, pointers are references to an array/list indexes. By using two pointers, we can process two elements at a time in a single loop. The two pointers iterate over an array/list in certain directions until some conditions are fulfilled and process two index elements simultaneously. The pattern is often used when - )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [1]
