/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (      Balance the heaps - The difference between the number        of elements in the Min Heap and the Max Heap should        not exceed 1. This ensures that the median will always be        at the root of either the Min Heap or the Max Heap \(or        the average of the roots if the heaps have equal size\).)
/E (      Balance the heaps - The difference between the number        of elements in the Min Heap and the Max Heap should        not exceed 1. This ensures that the median will always be        at the root of either the Min Heap or the Max Heap \(or        the average of the roots if the heaps have equal size\).)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
2826 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (      Accessing the median -        - If both heaps have the same number of elements, the          median will be the average of the roots of the two         heaps.       - If the heaps have different sizes, the median will be the          root of the heap with more elements.)
/E (      Accessing the median -        - If both heaps have the same number of elements, the          median will be the average of the roots of the two         heaps.       - If the heaps have different sizes, the median will be the          root of the heap with more elements.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
endobj
2827 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (      Inserting elements -       - Compare the new element with the current median.       - If the new element is smaller than or equal to the           current median, insert it into the Max Heap.       - If the new element is greater than the current median,           insert it into the Min Heap.)
/E (      Inserting elements -       - Compare the new element with the current median.       - If the new element is smaller than or equal to the           current median, insert it into the Max Heap.       - If the new element is greater than the current median,           insert it into the Min Heap.)
/Pg 34 0 R
>>
endobj
2828 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (      Rebalancing the heaps -       - After inserting the element, check if the difference          between the sizes of the two heaps is greater than 1.       - If it is, remove the root of the larger heap and insert it          into the smaller heap to maintain balance.)
/E (      Rebalancing the heaps -       - After inserting the element, check if the difference          between the sizes of the two heaps is greater than 1.       - If it is, remove the root of the larger heap and insert it          into the smaller heap to maintain balance.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [4]
>>
